  "claim_boundary": "Finite-grid robustness and partial-identification are distinct. The formal direct-only native-nonendemic North–Tropical vector difference is robust in 1541/1575 predeclared joint finite-grid cells, but it is not identified across the deterministic partial-identification envelope. Palearctic accessibility is the most observation-robust branch: 1575/1575 direct-only native-nonendemic finite-grid cells are robust and its sign remains positive across the direct-only envelope, although FDR support is not identified across every direct-only corner. Tropical accessibility is observation-fragile: finite-grid robustness is 1269/1575 in direct-only native non-endemics and its partial-identification interval crosses zero. Grid fractions are not probabilities, and no latent true completeness or pollinator mechanism is identified."
